From c62cdb6c3b226b34717466488a3a78fceaa54b70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Vis <118430440+mark-vis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 22:32:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/28] (b) v2, part b-3: \caption* with a replaced \@caption,
 no class change

\caption* skipped the step and then called \@caption. Classes and
packages that replace \@caption by a definition that does not know the
star (llncs, mwart/mwrep/mwbk, jpsj2, turabian-thesis, ...) then printed
the label with the number of the previous caption and wrote a list entry
("Fig. 1. First / Fig. 1. Starred", list entry "1 Starred"), worse than
the old garbage (review finding H2).

Now \caption* calls \@caption through \@caption@star, which lets
\fnum@<type> be \@caption@nolabel and makes \addcontentsline a no-op
while \@caption runs. A replaced \@caption that uses these two commands
as the kernel did then gives a caption without label and without list
entry, in the layout of the class. The kernel \@caption undoes the
settings at its start (\@caption@star@restore), so hooks and plugs see
the normal definitions; \@caption@star undoes them after the call
otherwise. \if@captionstar is not reset after a replaced \@caption, so
a deferred kernel \@caption (threeparttable) still sees the star.

The label for \caption* is \@caption@nolabel instead of an empty
argument: it typesets nothing and removes a colon that follows it
directly. So \@makecaption definitions of the form #1: #2 (the
standard classes and the many classes that copied them) show neither
label nor separator without any change. Other separators stay; such a
\@makecaption should test \if@captionstar.

The change of classes.dtx from (b) v1 (no ": " for an empty label) is
reverted: any change of the standard \@makecaption breaks packages that
compare it with the standard definition. babel-french then no longer
replaces the separator, so French documents with pdfLaTeX got
"Figure 1: text" instead of "Figure 1 - text" (caption suite,
test/babel/french-0, -4, -5); caption3 reports an unknown class.

Packages that replace \caption itself (hyperref without
\DocumentMetadata, float, beamer) bypass the kernel; documented.

Documentation: ltfloat.dtx (\caption* with classes and packages, the
label \@caption@nolabel), latex-lab-float.dtx (comment on the label),
draft sections for usrguide (Captions without a number) and clsguide
(Captions and \caption*).

Tests: caption-interface-001: article's \@makecaption with the label of
\caption*, \caption* with a class-like \@caption, with a wrapper of the
kernel \@caption and with a deferred kernel \@caption. float-024:
\caption* with hyperref's plugs.
float-025/026 (from (c)): the class \@makecaption gets the label
\@caption@nolabel for \caption*.
